'' RUN: a ustring concatenation passed to a ustring parameter is copied into a real
'' descriptor, called on and deleted. 'byref': the callee's first 'len( u )' consumed the
'' temporary ('5: 0: []'), and it leaked. 'byval': it went through fb_UStrAssignToA and the
'' callee read a narrow string as UTF-16. Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/ustring-concat-arg.bas -o tests/codegen/ustringconcatarg.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/ustringconcatarg.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  5: 5: [ABCFG]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  4<xyxy>
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  3<ABz>
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: done
